der'=>'Provider','-- Select a Provider --'=>'-- Select a Provider --','Amazon S3'=>'Amazon S3','Google Cloud Storage'=>'Google Cloud Storage','Bunny.net'=>'Bunny.net','DigitalOcean Spaces'=>'DigitalOcean Spaces','Wasabi'=>'Wasabi','Backblaze B2'=>'Backblaze B2','Cloudflare R2'=>'Cloudflare R2','Linode Object Storage'=>'Linode Object Storage','Custom S3-Compatible Storage'=>'Custom S3-Compatible Storage','Select your cloud storage provider. Regions are automatically detected or configured based on your bucket endpoint.'=>'Select your cloud storage provider. Regions are automatically detected or configured based on your bucket endpoint.','Credentials'=>'Credentials','Connection Method'=>'Connection Method','Define access keys in wp-config.php (recommended)'=>'Define access keys in wp-config.php (recommended)','Store access keys in the database (less secure but easier)'=>'Store access keys in the database (less secure but easier)','<strong>wp-config.php:</strong> More secure, credentials not stored in database. <strong>Database:</strong> Easier to manage but credentials stored in database.'=>'<strong>wp-config.php:</strong> More secure, credentials not stored in database. <strong>Database:</strong> Easier to manage but credentials stored in database.','Copy the following snippet to near the top of your wp-config.php and replace the stars with your keys.'=>'Copy the following snippet to near the top of your wp-config.php and replace the stars with your keys.','More info'=>'More info','Note:'=>'Note:','Replace \'aws\' with your provider (aws, google-cloud, bunny, digitalocean, wasabi, backblaze, cloudflare-r2, linode, or custom). For Google Cloud Storage, use \'gcs-json\' instead of access keys. For Bunny.net, use bunny-specific keys (see documentation).'=>'Replace \'aws\' with your provider (aws, google-cloud, bunny, digitalocean, wasabi, backblaze, cloudflare-r2, linode, or custom). For Google Cloud Storage, use \'gcs-json\' instead of access keys. For Bunny.net, use b